  "recordingMethod": "Chromium 151 CSS-pixel capture of two independent inert replays (local and opponent) of the checked-in sole-bench addDamageCounter, updateDamageCounter, addAbilityCounter, rotateCard, marker removal, wrapper MutationObserver, and bench ResizeObserver behavior. Checked-in HTML/CSS and cardback bytes are served through a deny-by-default route; the networked application module is stubbed and the digest-pinned DOM mutations are narrowly transcribed. Canonical UI and movement sources establish that special conditions are active-only and are removed during movement into bench. Marker creation and each q0 -> q1 -> q2 -> q3 -> q0 rotation are synchronous; native observer and window listener activity are counted separately, and the source ResizeObserver is observed live before an explicit harness-only disconnect.",
